title: Authorizations › Queue › Cardinal payer signal
route: /authorizations
intro: The one banner on the queue: a single compact line about a payer trend, its info icon, the filter it switches on, and the ways to turn the filter off or hide the banner.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: the banner text and which four requests it affects (I-2207, I-2218, I-2271 at Site B and I-2236 at Site A) are seed data. Nothing re-scores the requests live. The count in the banner is the affected requests at the sites in view: Both sites four, Site A one, Site B three.
---
screen q "Authorizations queue"
decision d0 "Are any open requests at the sites in view affected, and is the banner still shown?"
endx e0 "No banner\nNone affected, or you dismissed it"
screen bn "One-line banner: 'Payer signal. Cardinal Health Plan: 31% more IOP continued-stay denials this week.'\nInfo icon, 'Review the four', X"
click inf "Hover or focus the info icon 'More about this signal'"
overlay tip "Tooltip: 'The denials were mostly for thin recertification evidence. Four of your open requests are affected, and the agents have re-scored them.'\nEsc closes it"
process wd "Wording follows the count in view\n'Review the three' for three; for one the button reads 'Review it', the tip 'One of your open requests is affected ... re-scored it' and the chip 'Showing the request affected by the Cardinal signal'"

click r "Click 'Review the four'"
store sf "Payer-signal filter turns on"
screen ls "Queue lists only the four affected requests\nHeader: '4 of 56 open requests match these filters.'"
screen chip "Chip under the filters\n'Showing the 4 affected by the Cardinal signal'"
screen bb "Banner button now reads 'Show all requests'"

click sa "Click 'Show all requests'"
click cx "Click the X on the chip\n'Remove the Cardinal signal filter'"
click cf "Click 'Clear filters'"
click tl "Click a figure that is the only filter on,\nor click another figure (it replaces every filter)"
process off "Payer-signal filter turns off\nAll bands return, chip goes, button reads 'Review the four' again\nThe address loses ?signal=1"

click dis "Click the X on the banner\n'Dismiss signal'"
store hid "Banner stays hidden for the session\nuntil the demo data is reset"
process stay "If the filter was on, it stays on\nThe chip and 'Clear filters' still turn it off"

click op "Click 'Open' on an affected request"
goto gC "Continues in: Authorizations › Case page › Ways in"
process sh "When an affected request is signed and sent, it leaves the queue\nThe number in the banner drops"

q --> d0
d0 -->|No| e0
d0 -->|Yes| bn --> wd
bn --> inf --> tip
bn --> r --> sf --> ls
sf --> chip
sf --> bb
bb --> sa --> off
chip --> cx --> off
ls --> cf --> off
ls --> tl --> off
bn --> dis --> hid --> stay
ls --> op --> gC
ls -.-> sh
